# two-plane-records — the control plane's record types, one `<path>::<Type>` per line.
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# two-plane reads each type's named fields and reports one whose name is planning data. A
# line naming a file or braced struct the tree does not have is a refusal, never a pass: an
# unread record is indistinguishable from a clean one. A new control-plane record type is
# added here in the change that defines it.
